Z||000016||Formula||08-24-2001||09:53 PM||||I started this one.... does anyone want to hear the anymore?<P>				Intro<BR>	"That things never gonna run, boy!" says Dave to Chuck as he firmly presses the aluminum Mt. Dew can in his large palm while the pinging of the crunch echoes through the countryside.   "It may look like a rusty pile of sh*t now, dude, but it's gonna smoke yer a$$," Chuck firmly replies to Dave.  Dave swiftly turns towards the old beat down automobile, smoothly runs his hand over a rusty area on the holy fender, grins like a kid in a candy store, brushes a small brown section of the door so that flakes of rust slide off, and effortlessly breaks off a piece of old american iron.  "Naw!" says Dave.  Dave, then, kicks up some leaves with the new leather Nike shoes and heads towards his bright red car.  Dave chuckles and says, "call me when its time," and opens the exotic cars door towards the sky and climbs into the supporting leather seat. He buckles up, then, he runs his sweaty index finger over the yellow emblem and whispers to himself, "Never."<P>	Chuck stands on the smooth grey pavement and listens to the rumble of the six liter aluminum v-12 play a raspy tune and waves to dave while the exotic quickly speeds away.   Chuck leans against the beat up fender, patting it on the hood, and mumbles "You'll see." He gazes at the dawning sun and starts to work on the muscle car again.  <BR>					Section 1<BR>	Bzzzzzzz, Bzzzzzzzzz, Bzzzzzzzzz....."Damnit!" Chuck says as he trips trying to get to the phone that woke him up several seconds ago.  "Yello?" Chuck answers, "Hey, this's Jason, your motors done ands ready to go." Chuck replies "SWEET, I'll be right over!" <BR>	Walking into the greasy shop, Chuck raises his strong hand, yells "Hey!", and gets a big grin.  He jogs over to Jason, who is sitting by an orange chevrolet block, and turns the water pump pulley.  "Whats this thing makin?"asks Chuck, Jason replies,  "more then what yer grandaddys buck hooks!", Chuck with a puzzling look, nods his head and smiles.  Chuck stares Jason in the eye and whispers "Diablo?" Jason stares back and states, "sure thing."   "Lets get this thing home!" Chuck says, and Jason grabs some keys.  ||||reg||1
